1. Required Backtest Coverage

To avoid overfitting to a single market cycle or SEBI regulatory regime, your Silver/Gold historical replay layer should meet these baselines:
• Date Range (Minimum 7–10 Years: 2017–2026):
	• Why 2017+: Captures multiple full market cycles—including the 2018 mid-cap correction, the March 2020 COVID crash (extreme VIX > 80 tail risk), the 2020–2021 low-IV bull run, the 2022 global rate-hike sideways grind, and the post-2024/2025 SEBI F&O regulatory changes (weekly expiry rationalization, increased contract sizes, and upfront margin rules).
	• Intraday vs. EOD split: Keep 7–10 years of 1-minute OHLCV for cash stocks and index futures, and at least 4–5 years of 1-minute option chain snapshots (post-2021, when NSE weekly options liquidity became structurally representative of current market microstructure).
• Universe (Point-in-Time Survivor-Bias-Free):
	• Breadth & Regime Universe: Historical constituents of the NIFTY 500 (including delisted, merged, or excluded stocks on each historical date to prevent survivorship bias).
	• Tradable Execution Universe: Historical NSE F&O eligible stocks (~180–220 names) plus NIFTY and BANKNIFTY index spot, futures, and weekly/monthly option chains (filtering strikes within ± 15% of spot to keep Bronze/Silver storage manageable).
• Minimum Number of Trades per Regime:
	• Statistical Floor: 100–150 independent trades per regime bucket (e.g., Low VIX Trending, High VIX Mean-Reverting, Event/Expiry) per strategy. Fewer than 50 trades leaves your Sharpe ratio and max drawdown vulnerable to 2–3 lucky outliers.
	• Tail-Risk / Hard-Gate Regime: At least 30–50 historical trigger events across distinct calendar years to verify that your circuit-breaker rules actually save capital rather than just blocking profitable bounce trades.

2. Required Performance & Latency Targets

Because you are trading via standard broker/institutional APIs (non-colocated HFT), your architecture should optimize for deterministic consistency (p99 latency) rather than raw microsecond speed:

Metric	Intraday / Options Execution Target	Swing / Positional Target	Architectural Requirement
Decisions per Second (Throughput)	50 – 500 decisions/sec (burst capacity at market open 09:15 IST & 15:00 IST)	1 – 20 decisions/sec	Vectorized evaluation (Polars/NumPy) over your active watchlist + active option strikes simultaneously.
Capture Latency (Exchange → Bronze)	< 50 ms (p95) / < 150 ms (p99)	< 1,000 ms	Async WebSocket consumer writing directly to an in-memory ring buffer / Kafka before disk persistence.
End-to-End Decision Latency (Tick → Order Sent)	< 150 – 250 ms (p99)	< 2 – 5 seconds	Live loop reads pre-computed Gold features from Redis/shared memory; never query disk/Parquet on the hot path.


Practical Safeguards for Options & Multi-Asset Execution

• Slippage & Liquidity Modeling in Backtests: Enforce a minimum open interest (OI) and bid-ask spread filter in your Silver option chain table; apply at least 1–2 ticks of slippage on index options and 3–5 ticks on stock options, as stock option spreads widen sharply during VIX spikes.
• Timestamp Synchronization (Clock Drift): Sync your ingestion servers via NTP/PTP against IST exchange timestamps so Bronze event_time vs. ingested_at accurately flags feed lag before your live loop fires an options order on stale spot prices.

